===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, pertaining to, or in accordance with the (usually high) standards of a [[profession]].
#: {{ux|en|The doctor is very '''professional''' in his manner.}}
#: {{ux|en|You should get '''professional''' advice about your tax liability.}} 
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|II|passage=His forefathers had been, as a rule, '''professional''' men&mdash;physicians and lawyers; his grandfather died under the walls of Chapultepec Castle while twisting a tourniquet for a cursing dragoon; an uncle remained indefinitely at Malvern Hill;{{nb...}}.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} [[expert|Expert]].
# Of an occupation, paid, especially so as to provide a [[livelihood]].
#: {{ant|en|amateur}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''professional''' musician, a '''professional''' footballer}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Steven Pifer|work=Five years after Crimea’s illegal annexation, the issue is no closer to resolution
|url=https://cisac.fsi.stanford.edu/news/five-years-after-crimea’s-illegal-annexation-issue-no-closer-resolution|publisher=The Center for International Security and Cooperation|date=18 March 2019|passage= The little green men were clearly '''professional''' soldiers by their bearing, carried Russian weapons, and wore Russian combat fatigues, but they had no identifying insignia. Vladimir Putin originally denied they were Russian soldiers; that April, he confirmed they were.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260624010701/https://cisac.fsi.stanford.edu/news/five-years-after-crimea%E2%80%99s-illegal-annexation-issue-no-closer-resolution|archivedate=24 June 2026}}
# {{lb|en|often pejorative}} Engaging in persistent behaviour that is exaggeratedly implied to be a full-time, paid occupation.
#: {{ux|en|Don't listen to him, he's a '''professional''' bullshitter.}}
#: {{ux|en|As a '''professional''' optimist, I always look on the bright side.}}

